Z||000000||fastonpumpgas||10-12-1999||01:35 AM||||Has anyone tried this?  will it stop my rear calipers from locking up?   Any info (difficulty, things to watch for, tips and tricks) that anyone ahs would definately be appreicated.  that 70 bucks a peice is insane, where as a rebuild kit is 14 dollars !!!!  thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||10-12-1999||02:54 AM||||Be very careful with the pistons;probably the highest tolerance,mechanical part on the whole car.If there's any corrosion on the pistons,it may be wise to get the rebuilt units.Just get everything really clean,brake fluid-soaked when assembling,and it should work fine.<BR>Hard to say exactly what it is making the rears lock,could be the master cylinder,air in the rear circuit,contaminated pads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastonpumpgas||10-12-1999||07:31 AM||||Do you know of a website that might give instrutions or do you think they should be in the kit?  I thought that them locking up was a common thing on fiero's , I was goin gto put grand am calipers on the back, but being I have a 4 speed I woul dlike to have the E-brake||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-12-1999||09:17 AM||||If you are asking these kind of questions I sugjest you buy rebuilt calipers from the local parts store.<P>There are several things that need to be inspected very carfully. Instruction sheets and even pictures won't safely answer your questions. Plus you must properly hone out the cylinder. If you mess this up the pistons will leak. Of course honing requires a decent caliper bore to start with. If you don't know how to check the bore for out of round and other conditions then again,,, the pistons will likely leak.<P>and actually, you rear lockup problem could be the front calipers binding. If the fronts bind you have to hit the pedal harder. That locks up the rears.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-12-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||10-12-1999||11:10 PM||||Auto Zone sells rebuilt rear calipers, lifetime guarantee, for $32 each (plus $80 refundable core charge).  ||||reg||1
